### Complete Generation Pipeline Example

Source: https://github.com/iptv-org/iptv/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/generators.md

This example demonstrates a full generation pipeline, including loading data, parsing streams, attaching guides, and initializing various generators. It shows how to use `Storage`, `PlaylistParser`, and different generator classes.

```typescript
import { loadData, data } from './api'
import { PlaylistParser } from './core'
import { Storage } from '@freearhey/storage-js'
import * as generators from './generators'

async function generate() {
  // 1. Load reference data
  await loadData()

  // 2. Parse existing streams
  const streamsStorage = new Storage(STREAMS_DIR)
  const parser = new PlaylistParser({ storage: streamsStorage })
  const files = await streamsStorage.list('**/*.m3u')
  let streams = await parser.parse(files)

  // 3. Attach guides
  streams = streams.map(stream => {
    stream.setGuides(data.guidesGroupedByStreamId.get(stream.getId()))
    return stream
  })

  // 4. Generate all playlists
  const logFile = new File('generators.log')
  const generatorList = [
    new generators.RawGenerator({ streams, logFile }),
    new generators.CategoriesGenerator({ categories: data.categories, streams, logFile }),
    new generators.CountriesGenerator({ countries: data.countries, streams, logFile }),
    // ... etc
  ]

  for (const gen of generatorList) {
    await gen.generate()
  }
}
```

