### Typical IPTV API Integration Pattern

Source: https://github.com/iptv-org/iptv/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/api-interface.md

Demonstrates a common workflow for integrating the IPTV API into scripts. This includes loading data, accessing reference data, performing lookups, searching channels, and checking blocklists.

```typescript
import { loadData, data, searchChannels } from './api'
import { Stream } from './models'

// 1. Load all data
await loadData()

// 2. Access reference data
for (const country of data.countries.all()) {
  console.log(`${country.flag} ${country.name}`)
}

// 3. Look up specific items
const channel = data.channelsKeyById.get('us.nbc')
const feeds = data.feedsGroupedByChannel.get('us.nbc')

// 4. Search
const newsChannels = searchChannels('News')

// 5. Check blocklist
const records = data.blocklistRecordsGroupedByChannel.get('us.nbc')
if (records && records.some(r => r.reason === 'dmca')) {
  console.log('Channel is on DMCA blocklist')
}
```

